Sentence 3: Umbrella Movement
Umbrella Movement The Umbrella Movement () was a political movement that emerged during the Hong Kong democracy protests of 2014.
Sentence 4: Its name arose from the use of umbrellas as a tool for passive resistance to the Hong Kong Police during a 79-day occupation of the city demanding freer election, which was sparked by the decision of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress (NPCSC) of 31 August 2014 that prescribed a selective pre-screening of candidates for the 2017 election of Hong Kong's chief executive.
Sentence 5: On 6 December 2014, Cheng established Student Front, a student activism organization to fight against the "stage power" and to continue staying in the front line after the Hong Kong Federation of Students and Scholarism quit the protests.

