Sentence 1: Bhangra (dance)
Bhangra (dance) The term Bhaṅgṛā (</small>, ; pronounced Listen) refers to the traditional dance from the Indian subcontinent originating in the Majha area of the Punjab region.
Sentence 2: The origins of traditional Bhangra are speculative.
Sentence 3: According to Dhillon (1998), Bhangra is related to the Punjabi dance 'bagaa', which is a martial dance of Punjab.
Sentence 4: The traditional form of Bhangra danced in the villages of Sialkot district is regarded as the standard.
Sentence 5: Bhangra (; pronounced ) and Giddha are forms of dance and music that originated in the Punjab region.
Sentence 6: "Bhangra" dance began as a folk dance conducted by Punjabi farmers to celebrate the coming of the harvest season.
Sentence 7: The specific moves of "Bhangra" reflect the manner in which villagers farmed their land.
Sentence 8: This hybrid dance became "Bhangra".
