Sentence 5: In 1994, the game and puzzle division of Western Publishing was purchased by Hasbro (parent company of Parker Brothers, the makers of Monopoly) who were then controlling 80% of the U.S. board game market, and they chose to market a Star Wars Monopoly edition instead of SolarQuest.
Sentence 6: The Monopoly brand was thus strengthened, while SolarQuest was effectively blocked from the board game market.
