Sentence 3: Angle Inlet, Minnesota
Angle Inlet, Minnesota Angle Inlet is a census-designated place (CDP) and unincorporated community in Angle Township, Lake of the Woods County, Minnesota, United States.
Sentence 4: The community is part of the Northwest Angle, the only place in the contiguous United States north of the 49th parallel; it is the northernmost census-designated place in the contiguous United States.
Sentence 5: It borders Canada and is, together with a similar smaller cape to the west, separated by land from the continental United States.
Sentence 6: Except for minor surveying errors, it is the only place in the United States outside Alaska that is north of the 49th parallel, which forms the border between the U.S. and Canada from the Northwest Angle
