Sentence 2: Gordonia (plant) Gordonia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Theaceae, related to "Franklinia", "Camellia" and "Stewartia".
Sentence 3: Gordonia (plant)
differs in being deciduous and flowering in late summer, not late winter.
Sentence 4: The draft "Flora of China" account of Theaceae in China splits "Gordonia" into two genera, with "G. lasianthus" retained in "Gordonia", and the Asian species transferred to "Polyspora"; this treatment is not yet widely accepted.
Sentence 5: "Gordonia chrysandra" may have anti-inflammatory medicinal properties.
Sentence 6: There are about 40 species, including: Gordonia species from East Asia were transferred to Polyspora, including: Several species of "Gordonia" are grown as ornamental plants for their flowers produced in winter when few other trees are in flower.
