Sentence 1: Gates County, North Carolina
Prior to the American Civil War, most of Gates County was covered with virgin timber.
Sentence 2: In 1861, A. J. Walton was chosen as Gates County's representative to the North Carolina secession convention.
Sentence 3: After North Carolina voted to secede, the "Gates Guard" company was formed raised to protect its borders.
Sentence 4: However, Gates County's greatest contribution was in supplying food to the Confederate States Army.
Sentence 5: Brigadier General Laurence S. Baker, another Gates County native, lost an arm in the war.
