Sentence 1: Cooperative pulling paradigm
competing hypotheses regarding cooperation in wolves ("Canis lupus") and dogs.
Sentence 2: On the one hand, it could be theorized that dogs have been selected, during domestication, for tame temperaments and an inclination to cooperate and therefore should outperform wolves on a cooperative pulling task.
Sentence 3: On the other hand, it could be argued that dogs have evolved to become less able to work jointly with other dogs because of their reliance on humans.
Sentence 4: Wolves rely on each other for hunting, raising young and defending their territory; dogs rarely rely on other dogs.
