Sentence 1: Unalakleet, Alaska
Unalakleet, Alaska Unalakleet ( ; ) is a city in Nome Census Area, Alaska, United States, in the western part of the state.
Sentence 2: Unalakleet is known in the region and around Alaska for its salmon and king crab harvests; the residents rely heavily on caribou, ptarmigan, "oogruk" (bearded seal), and various salmon species.
Sentence 3: Unalakleet is also known for its aesthetic value, as it resides right next to the Bering Sea, immediately next to a large, clean river (Unalakleet River) and has trees, tundra, and hills behind it.
