Sentence 4: The name "Titanopsis" comes from the ancient Greek "titanos" (limestone) and "opsis" (looking like) The genus has a disjunct distribution, occurring in three separate areas of southern Africa: southern Namibia, the region around the south-eastern border of Namibia and a larger area spanning between the former Cape Province and Orange Free State in South Africa.
