Sentence 1: Westport Airport (Kansas)
Westport Airport (Kansas) Westport Airport is a privately owned, public use airport located three nautical miles (6 km) southwest of the central business district of Wichita, a city in Sedgwick County, Kansas, United States—and is in the Class C airspace of neighboring Wichita Dwight D. Eisenhower National Airport.
Sentence 2: NOTE: Westport is under the Class C controlled airspace for Wichita's nearby municipal airport -- Wichita Dwight D. Eisenhower National Airport (formerly Mid-Continent International Airport), which has extensive jet aircraft traffic (particularly business jets, which are built locally), and limited amounts of heavy aircraft traffic, as well as substantial traffic of general aviation airplanes and helicopters.
