Sentence 2: Bayan (accordion)
Bayan (accordion) The bayan () is a type of chromatic button accordion developed in Russia in the early 20th century and named after the 11th-century bard Boyan.
Sentence 3: The bayan differs from western chromatic button accordions in some details of construction: The differences in internal construction give the bayan a different tone color from Western instruments, and the bass has a much fuller sound.
Sentence 4: Because of their range and purity of tone, bayans are often the instrument of choice for accordion virtuosi who perform classical and contemporary classical music.
