Sentence 2: The Mark-8 was designed by graduate student Jonathan Titus and announced as a 'loose kit' in the July 1974 issue of "Radio-Electronics" magazine.
Sentence 3: The Mark-8 was introduced as a 'build it yourself' project in "Radio-Electronics"'s July 1974 cover article, offering a US$5 booklet containing circuit board layouts and DIY construction project descriptions, with Titus himself arranging for $50 circuit board sets to be made by a New Jersey company for delivery to hobbyists.
