Sentence 1: Home computer
Home computer Home computers were a class of microcomputers that entered the market in 1977, that started with what Byte Magazine called the "trinity of 1977", (the Apple II, the TRS-80 Model I, and the Commodore PET) and which became common during the 1980s.
Sentence 2: TRS-80 Model II
TRS-80 Model II The TRS-80 Model II was a computer system launched by Tandy in October 1979, and targeted at the small-business market.
Sentence 3: Despite its name, the Model II was not an upgrade of the original (Model I) TRS-80, but an entirely different system.
Sentence 4: The Model II was succeeded by the compatible TRS-80 Model 12, Model 16 and Model 16B and the Tandy 6000.
