Sentence 1: Bruno (bishop of Würzburg)
Bruno (bishop of Würzburg) Bruno of Würzburg (c. 1005 – 27 May 1045), also known as Bruno of Carinthia, was imperial chancellor of Italy from 1027 to 1034 for Conrad II, Holy Roman Emperor, to whom he was related, and from 1034 until his death prince-bishop of Würzburg.
Sentence 2: In 1026, Bruno was named regent in Germany during Conrad's expedition in Italy.
Sentence 3: Conrad had named Bishop Bruno of Augsburg regent of Germany while he marched south to Italy.
Sentence 4: Conrad returned to Germany in 1027, after being crowned Emperor, and held court at Augsburg in Swabia, calling upon the rebels to surrender.
