Sentence 1: West Triangle Economic Zone
West Triangle Economic Zone The West Triangle Economic Zone is an economic zone designated by the Chinese government comprising Chengdu, Chongqing and Xi'an.
Sentence 2: Created as part of China's Western Development strategy, the West Triangle Economic Zone contributes nearly 40% of Western China's GDP.
Sentence 3: The economies of all three cities are highly developed and serve as attractive investment locations within China.
Sentence 4: Shaanxi
is designated by Xi'an municipal government to exercise economic and administrative power within the zone.
Sentence 5: XEPZ is a special economic zone.
Sentence 6: By now, there are more than 40 enterprises home and abroad settled in XEPZ.
Sentence 7: The Western Triangle is a new economic zone composing the three major city-level economies of Western China: Xi'an, Chongqing and Chengdu.
Sentence 8: It is believed that the addition of Xi'an to the Triangle will spur economic growth in the region and allow the city an opportunity to capitalize on the commercial potential of its high-technology industries.
