Sentence 1: Europa (film)
Europa (film) Europa (known as Zentropa in North America) is a 1991 Danish art drama film directed by Lars von Trier.
Sentence 2: "Europa" was influenced by Franz Kafka's "Amerika", and the title was chosen "as an echo" of that novel.
Sentence 3: The film won the Golden Globe Award for Best Foreign Language Film and was nominated for the Academy Award: Best Writing Adapted Screenplay, but lost the award to "The Silence of the Lambs".
Sentence 4: It had been expected to be nominated for Best Foreign Language Film but Germany did not submit it.
